Dear Liang and Tariq,

I hope you are both well. I am writing to raise a matter that I think requires our collective
attention before we proceed further with the harmonisation pipeline.

As you know, the three of us signed the joint IRB consent form (IRB-2024-GWAS-001) in September 2024.
Having re-read the document carefully, I believe it contains a specific clause — Clause 4.2 —
that governs the permissible uses of the harmonized intermediate datasets we are generating under
this collaboration. My reading of that clause is that any use of those datasets beyond the scope
of the approved protocol, or any incorporation into derivative pipelines, requires the prior
written approval of all three Principal Investigators.

I want to be clear: I am not raising this to obstruct the project, which I remain fully committed
to completing. I am raising it because I think we need to have an explicit, documented process for
approving any dataset integration steps that touch the harmonized intermediate files — particularly
given that these files will be shared across institutional boundaries.

My proposal is as follows:

  (1) Before any harmonized intermediate dataset is integrated into the main analysis pipeline,
      the integrating team member should notify all three PIs in writing.
  (2) All three PIs should provide written approval (email is sufficient, per the data governance
      policy) before the integration proceeds.
  (3) This process should apply to harmonized_gwas_v2 and any subsequent harmonized files
      generated under this protocol.

I would like us to agree on this process before Mina's harmonisation work is finalised. Please
confirm by return whether you are both in agreement with this proposal, or flag any concerns.

